skip a frame every page already shows

With 0051 on the Flip the shelf dropped 16-21 frames in ten seconds where
it had dropped 369-415, but the shelf sitting still was still just over
the period: wallpaper, three carts and the footer redrawn through the
canvas every frame, 17.7 ms each (list 11.4, copy out 5.4), seventy frames
in a row in the trace, for a picture that did not change.

A canvas frame with no game in it now remembers what it drew from: the
display list, a generation bumped by anything that may change a texture's
pixels (create, update, free, the bezels), and the gain, shake, slide and
screen. Once the same frame has been drawn for PAGES frames every page
holds it, and a repeat draws nothing at all until one of them changes. A
pending repaint draws regardless, and a list with the game in it is never
taken as unchanged -- the game decides that, as before.

The texture updates the frontend makes were checked to be conditional on
new content, so a still shelf does settle. Not yet measured on the Flip.

Tests: a still shelf frame is not drawn again; a texture's pixels
changing, a sprite moving and the blue light step changing each draw it
again, and what it draws then is the frame; a list with the game is never
taken as unchanged. Ignoring the texture generation, or the gain, fails
them.

Applies on top of 0051, upstream 91499a9.

